    {
      "id": "scalar-adjoint-boundary-problem-standing-assumptions",
      "type": "ordinary-paragraph",
      "regions": [
        [
          321,
          80,
          720,
          955,
          930
        ]
      ],
      "en": "Throughout this subsection, let $L(\\bm{x},D)$ be a scalar elliptic differential operator of order $2m$ and let $B_j(\\bm{x},D)$, $j=1,\\ldots,m$, be boundary operators which satisfy the complementing conditions. The general theory of adjoints requires rather stringent regularity assumptions on $\\Omega$ and the coefficients; for simplicity we shall assume they are of class $C^\\infty$ and that $\\Omega$ is bounded. We make these assumptions throughout. We shall make the additional assumption that the $B_j$ are normal. This property is defined as follows.",
      "zh": "本小节始终设 $L(\\bm{x},D)$ 为 $2m$ 阶标量椭圆微分算子, $B_j(\\bm{x},D)$, $j=1,\\ldots,m$, 为满足补条件的边界算子. 伴随问题的一般理论要求 $\\Omega$ 和系数满足相当严格的正则性假设; 为简单起见, 假设它们属于 $C^\\infty$ 类且 $\\Omega$ 有界. 以下始终作这些假设. 还将附加假设 $B_j$ 正规. 这一性质定义如下.",
      "label": null,
      "render_role": "ordinary-paragraph",
      "source_locations": [
        {
          "pdf_page": 321,
          "printed_page": 311,
          "bbox": [
            31.980547112462006,
            287.85445356917245,
            381.7677811550152,
            371.8120025268478
          ],
          "bbox_precision": "visually selected parent block, top-left PDF points",
          "crop": "workspace/crops/chapter-09-batch-22/scalar-adjoint-boundary-problem-standing-assumptions-321.png",
          "raw_ocr": "workspace/raw-text/pdf-0321.txt"
        }
      ],
