    {
      "id": "normal-boundary-operators-definition",
      "type": "definition",
      "regions": [
        [
          321,
          80,
          940,
          955,
          1095
        ]
      ],
      "en": "The boundary operators $B_j(\\bm{x},D)$ are called normal, if their orders $m_j$ are different from each other and less than or equal to $2m-1$ and if, moreover, the leading-order term in $B_j$ contains a purely normal derivative, i.e., $B_j^p(\\bm{x},\\bm{n})\\ne0$ for every $\\bm{x}\\in\\partial\\Omega$ (here $\\bm{n}$ is the unit normal to $\\partial\\Omega$).",
      "zh": "若边界算子 $B_j(\\bm{x},D)$ 的阶数 $m_j$ 两两不同且不超过 $2m-1$, 并且 $B_j$ 的最高阶项含有纯法向导数, 即对每个 $\\bm{x}\\in\\partial\\Omega$ 都有 $B_j^p(\\bm{x},\\bm{n})\\ne0$ (这里 $\\bm{n}$ 是 $\\partial\\Omega$ 的单位法向量), 则称这些边界算子正规.",
      "label": "def:normal-boundary-operators",
      "render_role": "definition",
      "source_locations": [
        {
          "pdf_page": 321,
          "printed_page": 311,
          "bbox": [
            31.980547112462006,
            375.8099810486418,
            381.7677811550152,
            437.77864813644976
          ],
          "bbox_precision": "visually selected parent block, top-left PDF points",
          "crop": "workspace/crops/chapter-09-batch-22/normal-boundary-operators-definition-321.png",
          "raw_ocr": "workspace/raw-text/pdf-0321.txt"
        }
      ],
      "formula_ids": [
