    {
      "id": "dirichlet-boundary-system-definition",
      "type": "definition",
      "regions": [
        [
          321,
          80,
          1300,
          955,
          1450
        ]
      ],
      "en": "The boundary operators $F_j(\\bm{x},D)$, $j=1,\\ldots,p$, are called a Dirichlet system of order $p$, if their orders $m_j$ cover all values from zero to $p-1$ and if, moreover, the leading-order term in $F_j$ contains a purely normal derivative, i.e., $F_j^p(\\bm{x},\\bm{n})\\ne0$ for every $\\bm{x}\\in\\partial\\Omega$ (here $\\bm{n}$ is the unit normal to $\\partial\\Omega$).",
      "zh": "若边界算子 $F_j(\\bm{x},D)$, $j=1,\\ldots,p$, 的阶数 $m_j$ 覆盖从零到 $p-1$ 的全部取值, 并且 $F_j$ 的最高阶项含有纯法向导数, 即对每个 $\\bm{x}\\in\\partial\\Omega$ 都有 $F_j^p(\\bm{x},\\bm{n})\\ne0$ (这里 $\\bm{n}$ 是 $\\partial\\Omega$ 的单位法向量), 则称这些边界算子为 $p$ 阶 Dirichlet 系统.",
      "label": "def:dirichlet-boundary-system",
      "render_role": "definition",
      "source_locations": [
        {
          "pdf_page": 321,
          "printed_page": 311,
          "bbox": [
            31.980547112462006,
            519.737207833228,
